# English-only content

All human-readable text in this repository must be **English only**.

## Allowed

- Latin letters, digits, and standard ASCII punctuation used in code and docs
- Common English typography in Markdown/JSON strings: em dash, curly quotes, arrow (→), multiplication sign (×)
- Comments, commit messages, rules, docs, JSON string values, and identifiers that are meant for humans

## Not allowed

- Non-English natural language (e.g. Cyrillic, CJK, Arabic)
- Emoji and decorative symbols used as language
- Mixing another language into user-facing strings “for convenience”

## Exception

The **`.manual/`** directory is excluded from this rule (operator notes in any language).

## Optional check

`npm run check:english` scans repository text outside `.manual/` when you want
automated help finding violations. It is not a required completion step.

Fix violations or move non-English material into `.manual/`.

## Authoring guidance

- Write new docs, questions, and protocol text in English
- Prefer ASCII quotes and `->` in machine-oriented JSON keys when possible
- Keep Jev `instructions` and `criteria` in clear English; one atomic claim per question
